<title>BRAZIL: SOCCER-LIBERTADORES CUP RESULTS/STANDINGS.</title>
<headline>SOCCER-LIBERTADORES CUP RESULTS/STANDINGS.</headline>
<dateline>RIO DE JANEIRO 1997-03-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Results of South</p>
<p>American Libertadores Cup first round matches played Friday.</p>
<p>Group One</p>
<p>In La Paz: Bolivar (Bolivia) 3 Cerro Porteno (Paraguay) 1</p>
<p>(halftime 2-0)</p>
<p>Scorers:</p>
<p>Bolivar - Marco Sandy (5), Miguel Mercado (38), Antonio</p>
<p>Vidal Gonzalez (89, penalty)</p>
<p>Cerro Porteno -  Richard Gomez (48).</p>
<p>Attendance: 20,000</p>
<p>Group Four</p>
<p>In Lima: Sporting Cristal (Peru) 1 Gremio (Brazil) 0 (1-0)</p>
<p>Scorer: Norberto Solano (6, penalty)</p>
<p>Group Five</p>
<p>In Montevideo: Penarol (Uruguay) 2 Millonarios (Colombia)</p>
<p>1 (1-0)</p>
<p>Scorers:</p>
<p>Penarol - Carlos Aguilera (31), Antonio Pacheco (47)</p>
<p>Millonarios - Ricardo Perez (84, penalty)</p>
<p>Attendance: 30,000</p>
<p>Standings (tabulate under played, won, drawn, lost, goals</p>
<p>for, goals against, points)</p>
<p>Group One</p>
<p> Bolivar			    3  3  0  0 11  2  9</p>
<p>Oriente Petrolero (Bolivia)  3  2  0  1  5  5  6</p>
<p> Guarani (Paraguay)	     3  1  0  2  3  8  3</p>
<p> Cerro Porteno		    3  0  0  3  1  5  0</p>
<p>Group Four</p>
<p> Sporting Cristal		 3  2  1  0  2  0  7</p>
<p> Gremio			     3  2  0  1  6  2  6</p>
<p> Alianza (Peru)		   3  1  1  1  1  4  4</p>
<p> Cruzeiro (Brazil)		3  0  0  3  1  4  0</p>
<p>Group Five</p>
<p> Penarol			    2  2  0  0  6  2  6</p>
<p> Millonarios			3  2  0  1  5  4  6</p>
<p> Deportivo Cali (Colombia)    1  0  0  1  1  2  0</p>
<p> Nacional (Uruguay)	     2  0  0  2  2  6  0</p>
<p>Note: top three in each first round group qualify for the</p>
<p>second round. Holders River Plate (Argentina) have a bye to</p>
<p>the second round.</p>
</text>
